<title>SWEDEN: Volvo aims to sell 230,000 cars in Europe.</title>
<headline>Volvo aims to sell 230,000 cars in Europe.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Volvo Cars, a unit of Swedish automotive group AB Volvo, said on Monday it aimed to sell nearly 230,000 cars in Europe in 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;Our aim is to increase our sales in Europe to nearly 230,000 cars compared to last year's volume of 216,100 cars,&quot; Volvo Car's spokesman Ulf Thorne told Reuters.</p>
<p>Volvo Car's sales in Spain, Finland and Norway rose in February. Last week the company reported two-figure jumps in sales in four other European countries.</p>
<p>-- Henrik Alberius, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
